    "explanation": "To both parties. The platform's GPS trace governs the distance (POL-RD-01): it measures 27.28 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff, against the booked optimal of 22.0 km on the trip record — an excess of 5.28 km, or 24.0% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass (greater than 20% of optimal, and greater than 0.8 km absolute), so a route deviation is established and the rider's claim is made out. I have used the trace figure of 27.28 km, not the rounded trip-record copy of 27.3 km.\n\nThe driver's defence is the CTE closure, and it is tested under POL-RD-03 and nothing else. Limbs (a) and (b) are satisfied: advisory ADV-20260907-070 is a genuine LTA DataMall HIGH-severity closure on the Central Expressway (CTE) towards AYE after Braddell Rd, active 20:44:02–22:14:32 on 2026-09-07, which intersects the optimal route and overlaps the trip window by 65.5 minutes. Limb (c) — the actual route must leave the optimal corridor before the affected segment and rejoin it after — is not established. The record's closest available test of that limb, the platform's advisory-area computation, is negative: 0 trace fixes fall inside the advisory geometry and the trace's nearest approach is 1,344.79 m. On the record as it stands the closure is not shown to be what produced this excess, so the exoneration does not attach and the deviation stands at the measured figure. I have not used the driver's counterparty statement to carry limb (c): POL-RD-03 names a traffic advisory, not a party statement, and the statement asserts a closure rather than admitting the route.\n\nThe remedy is arithmetic under POL-RD-02. The fare is METERED, so POL-RD-11 does not apply. Recomputed fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 × 22.0 + 0.28 × 30.0) × 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP = 29.50. Charged total = 35.02. Refund = 35.02 − 29.50 = 5.52, rounded up to SGD 5.55. That exceeds the 0.50 de minimis and is far below the 90% full-refund